From 73cb3628a929b65fe0bb01135fba04cf42056ca2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:22:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): refuse a non-finite work-offset placement by name

A work offset whose rotation quaternion carried NaN or infinite parts
(or a zero norm) fell through the #315 rotated-offset gate as
"unrotated", so it would post as if the offset had no rotation.

- posting: one classifier (offset_frame: Square / Rotated / NonFinite)
  feeds the gate; a non-finite origin or rotation is refused with its
  own named line.
- SetWcsOrigin: its non-finite / degenerate refusals now name the slot.
- project load: a WCS row with a non-finite or zero-norm placement is
  refused by name instead of landing as the identity.
- setup sheet: a rotated (or non-finite) offset states it under the
  offset line; unrotated offsets render byte-identical.

Pinned by tests/rotated_wcs.rs.

Fixes #327

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
